b:T2b3d,<p>This Shipping & Delivery Policy ("Policy") explains how orders placed through <strong>Smile Agri-Market Technologies Ltd</strong> ("Smile Agri-Market," "we," "our," or "us") are processed, shipped, delivered, and managed. This Policy applies to purchases made through <a href="https://smileagrimarket.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>https://smileagrimarket.com</strong></a>, our mobile applications, and related services (collectively, the "Platform").</p>
<p>By placing an order through the Platform, you agree to this Policy, our Terms & Conditions, Buyer Policy, Seller Policy, and Refund & Cancellation Policy.</p>
<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market connects buyers with farmers, suppliers, and other agricultural businesses. Depending on the product and location, deliveries may be arranged by:</p>
<ul><li>The seller</li><li>Smile Agri-Market</li><li>Approved logistics partners</li><li>Independent courier or freight providers</li></ul>
<p>This Policy outlines the responsibilities of all parties involved in the delivery process.</p>
<h2>2. Delivery Coverage</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may provide delivery services within:</p>
<ul><li>Nigeria</li><li>Other African countries (where available)</li><li>International destinations (where permitted by law)</li></ul>
<p>Delivery availability depends on:</p>
<ul><li>Product type</li><li>Seller location</li><li>Buyer location</li><li>Logistics partner coverage</li><li>Import/export restrictions</li><li>Biosecurity and quarantine requirements</li></ul>
<p>Some products may only be available for local or regional delivery.</p>
<h2>3. Order Processing</h2>
<p>After an order is placed:</p>
<ol><li>The seller receives the order.</li><li>Payment is verified where applicable.</li><li>The seller confirms product availability.</li><li>Products are prepared for dispatch.</li><li>Shipping arrangements are made.</li><li>The buyer receives order updates where available.</li></ol>
<p>Orders are typically processed during normal business days. Processing times may vary depending on the seller, product, and season.</p>
<h2>4. Processing Times</h2>
<p>Estimated processing times may vary by product category.</p>
<p>Typical examples include:</p>
<ul><li>Fresh produce: 1–3 business days</li><li>Farm inputs: 1–5 business days</li><li>Farm equipment: 2–10 business days</li><li>Custom or bulk orders: As agreed between buyer and seller</li></ul>
<p>These estimates are provided for guidance only and are not guaranteed.</p>
<h2>5. Delivery Timeframes</h2>
<p>Estimated delivery times depend on:</p>
<ul><li>Buyer location</li><li>Seller location</li><li>Shipping method</li><li>Customs procedures</li><li>Weather conditions</li><li>Public holidays</li><li>Road conditions</li><li>Availability of transportation</li></ul>
<p>Estimated delivery dates are not guaranteed and may change due to circumstances beyond reasonable control.</p>
<h2>6. Shipping Charges</h2>
<p>Shipping charges may depend on:</p>
<ul><li>Weight</li><li>Volume</li><li>Distance</li><li>Delivery speed selected</li><li>Product type</li><li>Cold-chain requirements</li><li>Insurance (if selected)</li></ul>
<p>Applicable shipping costs will generally be displayed before checkout.</p>
<h2>7. Delivery Address</h2>
<p>Buyers are responsible for providing:</p>
<ul><li>Accurate delivery addresses</li><li>Contact telephone numbers</li><li>Delivery instructions where necessary</li><li>Recipient information</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market is not responsible for delays or failed deliveries resulting from incorrect or incomplete address information provided by the buyer.</p>
<p>Additional delivery charges may apply if an order must be re-delivered due to inaccurate delivery information.</p>
<h2>8. Perishable Goods</h2>
<p>Many products sold through the Platform are perishable.</p>
<p>To preserve quality:</p>
<ul><li>Buyers should ensure someone is available to receive deliveries.</li><li>Products should be inspected immediately upon arrival.</li><li>Products should be stored according to any handling instructions provided.</li></ul>
<p>Failure to promptly receive or properly store perishable goods may affect eligibility for refunds or replacements.</p>
<h2>9. Cold Chain Requirements</h2>
<p>Certain products require refrigerated or temperature-controlled transportation.</p>
<p>Where applicable:</p>
<ul><li>Sellers and logistics providers are responsible for maintaining appropriate transport conditions until delivery.</li><li>Buyers should promptly refrigerate or otherwise store products after receipt.</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market is not responsible for spoilage caused after delivery due to improper storage by the buyer.</p>
<h2>10. Delivery Confirmation</h2>
<p>A delivery may be considered complete when:</p>
<ul><li>The recipient signs for the order.</li><li>Delivery is confirmed electronically.</li><li>A one-time verification code is provided, where applicable.</li><li>Delivery is completed at the agreed location in accordance with the delivery instructions.</li></ul>
<p>Where contactless delivery is offered, confirmation may include photographic evidence or other reasonable proof of delivery.</p>
<h2>11. Inspection Upon Delivery</h2>
<p>Buyers should inspect their order immediately upon delivery.</p>
<p>If products appear:</p>
<ul><li>Damaged</li><li>Spoiled</li><li>Incorrect</li><li>Incomplete</li><li>Contaminated</li><li>Materially different from the order</li></ul>
<p>the buyer should notify Smile Agri-Market as soon as reasonably possible and, where practical for perishable goods, within <strong>24 hours</strong> of delivery.</p>
<p>Supporting photographs or videos may be requested to assist with the investigation.</p>
<h2>12. Failed Deliveries</h2>
<p>A delivery may fail if:</p>
<ul><li>The recipient is unavailable.</li><li>The delivery address is incorrect.</li><li>Access to the property is restricted.</li><li>The recipient refuses delivery without a valid reason.</li></ul>
<p>Where a delivery cannot be completed, additional delivery charges, storage fees, or product disposal costs may apply, particularly for perishable goods.</p>
<h2>13. Delivery Delays</h2>
<p>Delivery delays may occur due to:</p>
<ul><li>Severe weather</li><li>Flooding</li><li>Road closures</li><li>Customs inspections</li><li>Government restrictions</li><li>Vehicle breakdowns</li><li>Labour disputes</li><li>Public emergencies</li><li>High seasonal demand</li><li>Other events beyond reasonable control</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market will make reasonable efforts to communicate significant delays where information is available.</p>
<h2>14. Risk of Loss</h2>
<p>Unless otherwise agreed or required by applicable law:</p>
<ul><li>Risk of loss or damage generally transfers to the buyer upon confirmed delivery at the agreed delivery location.</li><li>Ownership of goods transfers in accordance with the applicable sales agreement and after full payment has been received, unless otherwise agreed.</li></ul>
<p>This provision does not affect any mandatory consumer rights under applicable law.</p>
<h2>15. Partial Deliveries</h2>
<p>In some circumstances, an order may be delivered in multiple shipments.</p>
<p>This may occur due to:</p>
<ul><li>Product availability</li><li>Different warehouse locations</li><li>Multiple sellers</li><li>Transportation limitations</li></ul>
<p>Where practical, buyers will be informed if their order will arrive in separate deliveries.</p>
<h2>16. International Deliveries</h2>
<p>International orders may be subject to:</p>
<ul><li>Customs inspections</li><li>Import permits</li><li>Duties</li><li>Taxes</li><li>Quarantine requirements</li><li>Local agricultural regulations</li></ul>
<p>Unless otherwise stated, buyers are responsible for customs duties, import taxes, and regulatory charges imposed by the destination country.</p>
<h2>17. Restricted Products</h2>
<p>Some products cannot be shipped to certain destinations due to:</p>
<ul><li>Import restrictions</li><li>Agricultural quarantine laws</li><li>Biosecurity regulations</li><li>Hazardous material regulations</li><li>Local legal requirements</li></ul>
<p>Smile Agri-Market reserves the right to cancel or refuse shipments where delivery would violate applicable laws or regulations.</p>
<h2>18. Tracking Orders</h2>
<p>Where available, buyers may receive:</p>
<ul><li>Shipment confirmations</li><li>Tracking numbers</li><li>Estimated delivery updates</li><li>Delivery notifications</li></ul>
<p>Tracking availability depends on the logistics provider and shipping method used.</p>
<h2>19. Logistics Partners</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market may work with independent logistics providers to facilitate deliveries.</p>
<p>While we seek to partner with reliable providers, each logistics provider remains responsible for the transportation services it performs.</p>
<p>Smile Agri-Market is not responsible for losses or delays solely attributable to the independent acts or omissions of third-party logistics providers, except where liability arises under applicable law or our own actions.</p>
<h2>20. Delivery Disputes</h2>
<p>If a delivery issue arises, buyers should contact Smile Agri-Market promptly.</p>
<p>We may assist by:</p>
<ul><li>Reviewing delivery records.</li><li>Contacting the seller.</li><li>Contacting the logistics provider.</li><li>Reviewing tracking information.</li><li>Investigating the circumstances.</li></ul>
<p>Our involvement is intended to facilitate resolution and does not make Smile Agri-Market the carrier or seller unless expressly stated.</p>
<h2>21. Force Majeure</h2>
<p>Smile Agri-Market shall not be liable for delivery delays or failures caused by events beyond our reasonable control, including:</p>
<ul><li>Natural disasters</li><li>Epidemics or pandemics</li><li>War</li><li>Civil unrest</li><li>Government actions</li><li>Power failures</li><li>Telecommunications failures</li><li>Cybersecurity incidents</li><li>Transportation disruptions</li><li>Extreme weather conditions</li></ul>
<h2>22. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may revise this Shipping & Delivery Policy from time to time.</p>
<p>Material changes will be published on the Platform with an updated Effective Date.</p>
<p>Continued use of the Platform after changes become effective constitutes acceptance of the revised Policy.</p>
<h2>23. Governing Law</h2>
<p>This Policy is governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, without prejudice to any mandatory consumer protection rights that may apply in your jurisdiction.</p>
<h2>24. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have questions about shipping or delivery, please contact:</p>
<p><strong>Smile Agri-Market Technologies Ltd</strong></p>
<p>Website: <a href="https://smileagrimarket.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>https://smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>
<p>Customer Support: <a href="mailto:support@smileagrimarket.com"><strong>support@smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>
<p>Logistics Support: <a href="mailto:logistics@smileagrimarket.com"><strong>logistics@smileagrimarket.com</strong></a></p>6:["$","main",null,{"className":"container-page py-12 sm:py-16","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto max-w-3xl","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.7rem] font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground","children":"Legal"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl","children":"Shipping & Delivery Policy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":["Effective date: ","July 9, 2026"," · Last updated:"," ","July 9, 2026"]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"mt-10 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&_a]:font-medium [&_a]:text-leaf-600 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-4 [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h3]:mt-7 [&_h3]:text-base [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-ink [&_li]:mt-2 [&_ol]:mt-4 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-6 [&_p]:mt-4 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-ink [&_ul]:mt-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$b"}}],"$Lc"]}]}]
